{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "one-color rectangular frame, two parallel full-interior marker bars, and periodic source-color stripes between the bars",
  "dst": "same-size bg canvas with marker bars extended and the periodic stripe mask projected across the full grid",
  "transform": "infer the source stripe period along the axis perpendicular to the marker bars; paint those whole rows or columns with the frame color, extend the marker bars across the canvas, and repaint source-color cells between the bars"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14-19 rows x 15-19 cols, same-size output
  colors: 4 total -- bg (always 0), frame, bar, source; all distinct
  frame: 1-cell-thick border filling entire boundary row/col; color != 0 [observed]
  bar_color: always 3 [observed]; source_color: always 2 [observed]
  bars: 2 parallel full-interior lines of bar_color, either both rows (horizontal) or both cols (vertical)
  gap: on_count cells between the two bars (range 1-4); filled with source_color on selected periodic slices
  periodic_pattern:
    axis: perpendicular to bars (rows if vertical bars, cols if horizontal)
    unit: on_count consecutive 1s + off_count consecutive 0s (on 1-4, off 2-3, period = on+off = 3-6)
    inner alignment: unit[0] at inner index 0 (grid index 1); pattern may truncate at far edge
    source cells: on-slices between the two bars are filled with source_color; off-slices are bg
  remaining_interior: bg (0) everywhere inside the frame not occupied by bars or source stripes
  output_rule: |
    Remove frame. Extend bars to span full grid axis. Infer periodic mask from inner source pattern,
    extend it to full grid length (mask[i] = inner_unit[i % period] with offset 1 for the frame).
    Selected rows/cols get frame_color everywhere (except bar/source cols/rows keep their color).
    Non-selected rows/cols are bg. Source cells between bars on selected slices keep source_color.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick grid dims H x W in 14-19, orientation (horizontal or vertical), 4 distinct colors (bg=0, frame, bar, source)
    - Pick on_count (1-4), off_count (2-3); period = on + off
    - Build the periodic unit [1]*on + [0]*off; the full-grid mask is unit[(i-1) % period] for the stripe axis (length H or W)
    - Place two bar lines at arbitrary valid positions along the bar axis (gap = on_count cells between them)
    - Construct output directly -- bars span full grid, selected stripes get frame_color, source cells between bars on selected stripes
    - Derive input: wrap interior in a 1-cell frame of frame_color; inside, place bars and source stripes as they appear in the output interior; fill rest with bg
```
