  32:     - When a beam hits an obstacle, keep the obstacle unchanged and paint the available three-cell side wakes above and below it.
  33:     - A side wake is blocked if its left entry cell is an unactivated obstacle; obstacles reached inside wakes paint only their open side wakes and the cell immediately to their right.
  34:     - If a hit obstacle has obstacles at both forward diagonals, the original beam stops and full beams continue on those two adjacent rows without painting back through the parent obstacle.
  35: 
